.TH "SPGEN-BRUNO" "1" "" "spgen 0.1.0" ""
.SH NAME
spgen\-bruno \- Generates the Bruno API\-request documentation for an operation
.SH SYNOPSIS
mix sp.gen.bruno [options] <COMMAND|QUERY>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Runnable request documentation for one endpoint, in the Bruno collection at the repo root. Not a test: a thing you can click while developing the operation.
.SH Prerequisite
.IP \[bu] 2
The operation exists in the Domain Model (../../../../domain\-model/README.md); the controller and route are generated, so the path and verb are real.
.SH "What the generator does"
One file per operation at bruno/<Subdomain>/<Composite>/<Constituent>/<Operation Title>.yml, title\-cased like the rest of the collection, plus the constituent's folder.yml beside the first request it holds.
.IP \[bu] 2
Verb by element kind: POST for a command, GET for a query — the same rule the controller follows.
.IP \[bu] 2
URL against {{apiUrl}}; collection variables live in bruno/environments/.
.IP \[bu] 2
A JSON:API body mirroring the operation's data: create carries attributes only (the id is generated), update and delete address the row by id.
.IP \[bu] 2
examples: generated from the domain model's feature scenarios.
.IP \[bu] 2
seq: orders commands before queries, so assignment order matches the run order — run the command generators first.
.IP \[bu] 2
Docs artifacts are create\-only: an existing .yml is never rewritten, so hand\-tuned headers, saved responses and extra examples survive every run. An API change is therefore not propagated — when the operation's shape changes, update the file (or delete it and regenerate). See Ownership (../../README.md#ownership).
.SH Tests
None. Bruno files are documentation, not code under test — the endpoint they describe is tested in the endpoint test (./endpoint\-test.md).
.SS "Generated files"
.IP \[bu] 2
bruno/<Subdomain>/<Composite>/<Constituent>/<Operation Title>.yml (request docs per operation)
.IP \[bu] 2
bruno/<Subdomain>/<Composite>/<Constituent>/folder.yml (folder defaults for requests)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-subdomain\fR \fI<SUBDOMAIN>\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-composite\fR \fI<COMPOSITE>\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-constituent\fR \fI<CONSTITUENT>\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-model\fR \fI<MODEL>\fR
model root, default docs/domain\-model (relative to \-\-root)
.TP
\fB\-\-root\fR \fI<ROOT>\fR
repo root, default inferred from the current directory
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
report the drift, write nothing
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-force\fR
FE: rewrite present generated units in place
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fICOMMAND|QUERY\fR>
the element: esdm: reference, *.esdm.yaml, kind.name, or bare name
.SH "SEE ALSO"
spgen(1)
suites: endpoint, feature
